  finance export. Setting [38;5;153mverify=False[39m on the two [38;5;153mrequests.get[39m calls in [38;5;153mclient.py[39m turns off certificate validation for
  production too, which makes that nightly run interceptable by anyone who can MITM the connection (and it'll also emit
  [38;5;153mInsecureRequestWarning[39m on every call).

  The self-signed staging cert is a real problem worth solving; I just don't want to solve it by disabling TLS
  verification on the production path.

